# This file is generated from the metadata.xml of the packages.
# Do not edit by hand: run use-local-desc.py of the skill gentoo-overlay.
dev-libs/date:only-c-locale - Build only the C locale
gui-apps/swaync:pulseaudio - Build the volume widget of the control center with media-libs/libpulse
gui-apps/waybar:backlight - Enable module that controls the current backlight level
gui-apps/waybar:evdev - Enable libevdev support for evdev related features
gui-apps/waybar:experimental - Enable experimental features, such as Bluetooth battery reporting
gui-apps/waybar:libinput - Enable libinput support for libinput related features
gui-apps/waybar:logind - Enable support for logind (bluetooth and idle inhibit)
gui-apps/waybar:mpd - Enable support for the Music Player Daemon
gui-apps/waybar:mpris - Enable support for mpris
gui-apps/waybar:network - Enable libnl support for network related features
gui-apps/waybar:niri - Enable support for Niri Wayland compositor
gui-apps/waybar:pipewire - Enable support for pipewire
gui-apps/waybar:pulseaudio - Enable support for volume control via PulseAudio
gui-apps/waybar:sndio - Enable support for volume control via sndio
gui-apps/waybar:tray - Enable support for tray
gui-apps/waybar:wifi - Enable support for wifi/rfkill
gui-libs/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr:elogind - Enable support for rootless session via elogind
sys-boot/uconsole-pi-firmware:cm4 - For the Raspberry Pi CM4: also start4*.elf and fixup4*.dat of the firmware of Raspberry Pi
sys-boot/uconsole-pi-firmware:cm5 - For the Raspberry Pi CM5: config.txt and cmdline.txt only; its firmware is in the EEPROM
sys-kernel/uconsole-pi-kernel:cm4 - Build the kernel of the Raspberry Pi CM4 (bcm2711_defconfig, kernel8.img)
sys-kernel/uconsole-pi-kernel:cm5 - Build the kernel of the Raspberry Pi CM5 (bcm2712_defconfig, kernel_2712.img)
sys-kernel/uconsole-pi-kernel:cm5-16k - Also build the kernel of the CM5 with 16K pages, kernel_2712_16k.img, beside the kernel with 4K pages
sys-power/drowse:cm5-tuned - Install the profiles of sys-apps/tuned cm5-powersave and cm5-powersave-no-radio (a Raspberry Pi 5 or CM5 while idle) as profiles, not only as examples
sys-power/drowse:sway - Install /etc/sway/config.d/80-idlehint.conf: a gui-apps/swayidle that sets the idle hint of the session of sway for logind, which drowse needs
sys-power/drowse:waybar - Install the module of gui-apps/waybar and its style in /etc/xdg/waybar
virtual/linux-sources:firmware - Install the firmware of the kernel, sys-kernel/linux-firmware
